🚀 LEVEL 1 — Basic String Patterns (Beginner)

Focus: Character traversal, counting, simple string logic.
    ✅ LEVEL – EASY (Beginner to Intermediate Foundation)
    ⭐ Pattern 1: Traversal
            Print each character
            Print characters with index
            Count letters, digits, spaces, special chars
            Convert uppercase → lowercase and vice versa

   ⭐ Pattern 2: Reverse Patterns
            Reverse a string
            Reverse without extra space (char array)
            Reverse words in a sentence
            Reverse only vowels

   ⭐ Pattern 3: Frequency / Counting
            Count frequency of each character
            Count vowels/consonants
            Most frequent character
            First non-repeating character

   ⭐ Pattern 4: Palindrome-Based
            Check if string is palindrome
            Longest palindrome substring (Level 3)
            Remove characters to make palindrome

   ⭐ Pattern 5: Two-Pointer Patterns
            Remove duplicates in a string
            Skip adjacent duplicates
            Move vowels to the front/back
            Reverse only part of string

   ⭐ Pattern 6: Substring Patterns
            Print all substrings
            Longest substring without repeating characters
            Substring count based on rules

   ⚡ LEVEL – MEDIUM (Most Asked in Interviews)
   These problems test string algorithms, sliding window, hashing, indexing.

   ⭐ Pattern 7: Anagram Patterns
            Check if two strings are anagrams
            Group anagrams
            Check if substring is an anagram

   ⭐ Pattern 8: Sliding Window (Strings)
            Longest substring with K distinct chars
            Longest repeating character replacement
            Minimum window substring

   ⭐ Pattern 9: HashMap / HashSet Patterns
            Count distinct characters
            Check for repeated substring
            Detect duplicates

   ⭐ Pattern 10: Stack-Based Patterns
            Remove adjacent duplicates
            Decode strings like "3[a2[b]]"
            Check valid parentheses

   ⭐ Pattern 11: String Builder Patterns
            Remove characters efficiently
            Insert characters efficiently
            Build output strings for performance

   ⭐ Pattern 12: Numeric + String Mixed Patterns
            Convert string to integer
            Validate number
            Add two numeric strings

🔥 LEVEL – HARD (Advanced DSA on Strings)
    Used by MAANG, Adobe, Atlassian, Bloomberg for SDE/SDET 1–2.
   ⭐ Pattern 13: Prefix/Suffix String Patterns
            Longest prefix which is also suffix
            KMP prefix-function explanation
            Remove common prefix/suffix
   ⭐ Pattern 14: Sorting-Based String Patterns
            Sort characters inside string
            Sort words in a string
   ⭐ Pattern 15: Recursion-Based Patterns
            Reverse string using recursion
            Remove target character via recursion
            Generate all subsequences

   ⭐ Pattern 16: Bit Manipulation on Strings (rare but asked)
            Toggle case using bitmask
            Check uppercase/lowercase using bit operations


⭐ LEVEL 3 — ADVANCED STRING PATTERNS
    ⭐ Pattern 17: Dynamic Programming on Strings
            Longest Palindromic Subsequence
            Edit Distance
            Word Break problem
            Longest Common Subsequence
    ⭐ Pattern 18: Trie (Prefix Tree)
            Insert/Search words
            Auto-complete suggestions
            Count words with prefix

    ⭐ Pattern 19: Rabin-Karp / Z-Algorithm
            Pattern searching in O(n)
            Substring hashing